NAME
       grub2-editenv - show or change the GRUB environment block

SYNOPSIS
       grub2-editenv [FILE] list

DESCRIPTION
       GRUB keeps a few variables in a small file, the environment block, that
       it reads at every boot: /boot/grub2/grubenv on RHEL 9. The most
       important one is saved_entry, the id of the boot menu entry GRUB starts
       by default. FILE is the block to work on; use "-" (or leave it out) for
       the default file.

       The real tool can also change variables ("set NAME=VALUE", "unset
       NAME"), but there is rarely a reason to: grubby --set-default and
       grub2-set-default change saved_entry for you. On the RHCSA you
       normally only need "list" to look at it.

COMMANDS
       list   Print every variable as NAME=VALUE.

EXAMPLES
       See which entry boots by default:
              # grub2-editenv list
              saved_entry=da8d...-5.14.0-503.14.1.el9_5.x86_64
              menu_auto_hide=1
              boot_success=1

FILES
       /boot/grub2/grubenv

SEE ALSO
       grubby(8), grub2-set-default(8), grub2-mkconfig(8)
